      "content": "If it were a compliance test, researchers would be looking at subtle indicators of dissonance or assimilation in skeptical individuals. They'd measure things like participation persistence—how long someone stays engaged despite the absurdity—and the degree to which their body language aligns with the group energy. Metrics might also include rapid adoption versus hesitant joining, gauging the threshold of behavioral influence necessary to override personal skepticism.",
